WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.480
- Everything okay with you two?

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.313
- You and me?

00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:06.146
No, we're a mess.

00:00:06.146 --> 00:00:07.735
We should spend some time apart.

00:00:07.735 --> 00:00:10.152
(soft music)

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.360
- This woman named, Riswana,

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.993
I think I was actually speaking
with India, but anyway.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.070
And she found a box of the old ones

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.770
and they sent them free of charge,

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.210
and their exactly the right kind.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.580
- Wow that is a great story mom.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.510
- Oh, don't be a dick, honey.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.340
- You're not even
friends with Beth Chapin.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.173
- So what?

00:00:36.173 --> 00:00:37.130
You don't have to be friends with someone

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:37.963
to do what's right.

00:00:37.963 --> 00:00:40.900
- [Elsa] Sweetie, hitting
someone's face is never right.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.230
- Of course you don't get it.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.063
When you were in high school,

00:00:43.063 --> 00:00:44.280
you were the one picking on the fat kids.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.620
- I had a pudgy friend.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.680
Besides Bailey Bennett is a lovely girl,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.580
and she did not deserve to get punched.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.170
- Bailey Bennett is a twat.
- [Elsa] Card.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.261
- What's going on?

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:56.550
- I have to cancel the Visa.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.800
I left it at that bar after dance class.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.430
That's what you're
wearing, that sweatshirt?

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.384
- What's wrong with it?

00:01:02.384 --> 00:01:05.030
- Nothing, I just don't
understand why you do all

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.400
that working out if you're not going

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.960
to flaunt your cute little figure.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.620
- Oh my god mom, you want
me to dress sluttier?

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.840
- Why are you canceling it?

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.430
- Identity theft.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.150
Sweetie it was a compliment.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.810
You're adorable under all that bulk

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.290
- Bye.
(door slam)

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.123
- Hey guys
- Hey!

00:01:19.123 --> 00:01:20.910
- What did you think of the race?

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:21.850
- Great.

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.190
- You're so fast, you
were like a human car.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.330
- Yeah, vroom.
- Amazing.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.580
- You didn't see it?
- No, we didn't.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.170
Sam had a major incident.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.356
- He cut his hand.
- He was very upset.

00:01:33.356 --> 00:01:34.189
- Honey.

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:35.650
- I bought these churros
with my own money,

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:36.680
so you can't have one.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.240
Please don't ask.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.641
Hey!

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:43.500
(crunching)
- I didn't ask.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.161
- I feel like I keep
messing up with you, Casey.

00:01:46.161 --> 00:01:47.122
- It's okay.

00:01:47.122 --> 00:01:49.438
Don't worry about it,
Sam had a thing I get it.

00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:50.942
- Yeah, it was a bad thing.

00:01:50.942 --> 00:01:52.610
- Damn it, Casey.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.440
Hey Mrs. Gardener!

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:55.880
- Evan.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.866
Whoa, what a nice surprise.

00:01:57.866 --> 00:01:59.170
- Hey, hi, yeah.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.900
- We have cheese, help yourself, and figs.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.603
- Oh, love figs.
- All kids do.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.100
- Casey, this is a family dinner.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.570
I've been cooking all day,
this is important to me.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.100
Only you would invite someone

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.795
to a family dinner without even asking.

00:02:17.795 --> 00:02:21.200
Sam and friends,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.580
so many people.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.804
- This is awesome.

00:02:23.804 --> 00:02:27.350
- Zahid's my friend, and Paige
is just a girl from school.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.150
- Come on in, you know the drill.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.133
- I certainly do.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.823
So strong, thank you.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.210
- Well it's very nice to meet you all.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.460
- Evan.
- Mr. Gardener.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.293
- Dad.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.510
- Why are we all saying
each other's names?

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.690
- Hey guys, why don't
you go sit on the sofa

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.220
and talk amongst yourselves,
and I'll be there in a minute.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.960
Maybe tell an embarrassing
story about yourself

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.630
that nobody else knows.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.750
We did that as an icebreaker
at Sam's camp last summer,

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.893
and boy were there some red faces.

00:02:59.757 --> 00:03:02.424
(gentle music)

00:03:04.528 --> 00:03:08.670
- Don't you think that's a
little el doobich, blunt, kush.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:12.683
- Since its clearly bothering
you, why don't we just, honey.

00:03:13.604 --> 00:03:14.790
- I'm sorry, what?

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.010
- I'm just going to take it off.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:16.870
- What?

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.215
What the hell are you doing?

00:03:18.215 --> 00:03:20.961
(laughs)

00:03:20.961 --> 00:03:22.973
Are you serious?
- Yeah, great.

00:03:22.973 --> 00:03:23.806
Much better.

00:03:23.806 --> 00:03:24.830
- I kind of like the smell of smoke.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.140
Reminds me of my uncle Rasheed

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.400
when he gave me sips of his beer.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.147
- Oh my gosh, look at you!

00:03:31.055 --> 00:03:32.833
You look so pretty.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.623
Maybe different shoes.
- Mom.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.640
- Honey, I want you to know
that I am fully onboard

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.770
for you to attend Clayton Prep.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:46.900
- Are you?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:47.860
Does this have anything to

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.300
with the five hour
closed door conversation

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.600
that you and dad had the other day?

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.460
- It took me some time, but I got there.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.580
And the distance and the money,

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.990
and Sam, we'll figure it out.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.710
- Honey you've always been
so mature and sophisticated.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.320
You're going to fit right in here.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.670
- Mom, I punched a girl
in the face two weeks ago.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.740
- Honey they don't know that, okay.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.940
Look, look at that girl in
her little uniform marching

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.890
towards her future with that big backpack.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.060
That's going to be you next year.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.333
Fresh start.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.860
I got a fraud alert on my credit card.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.496
Did you have to pick the most
expensive dress in the store?

00:04:25.496 --> 00:04:27.377
(crying)
- Oh, honey.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.780
I'm joking, I'm just kidding you.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.113
(sniffling)

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.660
- I don't want to go to Clayton Prep.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:39.493
- Okay.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.170
- And honestly...

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.700
I don't know if I can
go because apparently

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.150
they found out that I
punched Bailey Bennett.

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.273
- Oh I know, I check in with them.

00:04:51.273 --> 00:04:53.740
- Then why are you like telling
people that I'm going to go

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.120
there and buying me shirts?

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.130
- Because I think you're amazing,

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.909
and I think you're going to get in anyway.

00:04:59.909 --> 00:05:02.387
- I'm just...

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.540
I'm scared because I don't
want to leave you guys

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.080
and Evan, and my team.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.450
The whole Clayton Prep thing is starting

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.420
to feel kind of like...

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.510
- Selfish.
- Yeah.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.670
- Yeah.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.130
- Even Sherice turned against me.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.240
- No, Sherice is your best friend.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.750
When you were little she used to follow

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.240
you around like a puppy dog.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.360
- No, she was the one
that stole my clothes.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.263
- She's a little bitch.
- I know.

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:32.028
(gentle music)

00:05:33.341 --> 00:05:37.549
- Honey, it's okay to be a little selfish.

00:05:37.549 --> 00:05:40.216
(gentle music)

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.443
- Thanks mom.

00:05:44.226 --> 00:05:45.710
- You kept the tags on right?

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.543
- Duh.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.940
- Hey sleepy head, there she is.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.370
I was thinking we should celebrate
you getting into Clayton.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.632
Maybe go out to breakfast,
just the two of us?

00:05:54.632 --> 00:05:56.540
(door slams)
Or lunch.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.123
(upbeat music)

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.040
- Hey Case, want me to do your hair?

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.260
I can squeeze you in.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.160
- Why are you even doing this?

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.010
You know Sam's not going
to the dance anymore.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.500
- Well whether he goes or not,

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.851
I made a commitment and I plan to keep it.

00:06:10.851 --> 00:06:12.620
- Oh really?

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.693
I didn't think commitments
mattered to you.

00:06:16.774 --> 00:06:19.120
- I'll be right back.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.280
Honey, I don't know
what's going on with you.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.900
If you're stressed about changing schools,

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.470
or if it's something else,

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:30.439
but you can't keep taking it out on me.

00:06:30.439 --> 00:06:31.639
I haven't done anything.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.563
- Yeah, you're perfect.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:36.863
- Hey.

00:06:40.393 --> 00:06:42.143
I love you very much.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:44.880
- Okay, whatever, I have to go.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:51.270
- Oh Casey, good news.
- Oh Elsa, I don't care.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.810
- Why are you calling Mom Elsa?

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.043
- Your Clayton uniform came today.

00:06:55.043 --> 00:06:57.930
I hung it in your closet to
get rid of that factory smell.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:00.223
But it is adorable.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.333
It just looks smart.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.770
So, what do you two think of the roast?

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.263
Just for fun I tried a new
pre-packaged spice mix.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:13.400
- Cheater.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.310
- Why did you change the spice mix?

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.850
Also, Elsa, you carved it weird.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.610
Dad carves it better,
when is he coming back?

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:21.620
Do we call him Doug?

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.100
- No, we're still Mom and Dad.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.710
- Yeah that's a good question.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.840
When is Dad coming home?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.340
- Well, he's at Grandpa's
building the porch.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.760
So, whenever that's done.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.130
- Well, I guess that's good

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.840
that he's building a home
instead of wrecking one.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.323
- Who wants more carrots?
- Hard pass.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.200
- Going for a run.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:43.843
- Hey you two.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.043
You look cozy.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:48.860
- What?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.420
- I'm just coming in to see
if anyone wanted a snack

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:52.624
or something to drink?

00:07:52.624 --> 00:07:55.280
- We're good actually.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.300
- Oh no, that blazer is a little big.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:59.290
You should let me tailor it.
- No thanks.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.420
- I'll just take it in a smidge.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.760
- Please don't.
- Just a skoush.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:02.593
- Bye lady.

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:06.205
- Yeah, get out of here.

00:08:06.205 --> 00:08:10.456
Sorry, sorry.
(soft music)

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.706
(thudding)

00:08:13.912 --> 00:08:16.014
(frustrated exhaling)

00:08:16.014 --> 00:08:18.051
(hip hop music)

00:08:18.051 --> 00:08:18.884
(grunts)

00:08:18.884 --> 00:08:19.717
- Huh?

00:08:19.717 --> 00:08:21.766
(hip hop music)

00:08:21.766 --> 00:08:23.717
- Great, now there's two of you.

00:08:25.094 --> 00:08:25.927
- Mom?

00:08:25.927 --> 00:08:28.885
(hip hop music)

00:08:28.885 --> 00:08:30.510
- Oh good, you're up.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.177
(hip hop music)

00:08:34.627 --> 00:08:36.852
We have a lot to talk about young lady.

00:08:36.852 --> 00:08:39.519
(hip hop music)

00:08:40.665 --> 00:08:43.500
♪ What I know, I know ♪

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.640
- Arlo is such a shitbag!
- Casey.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.505
- No she's right, that kid is a shitbag.

00:08:47.505 --> 00:08:48.970
- Shitbag or not,

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.140
oh it does feel gross
to say that out loud.

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:52.343
- I find it invigorating, shitbag.

00:08:52.343 --> 00:08:54.740
- We have to handle this calmly.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.960
- Okay, well, I am gonna
calmly go over to his house and

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.099
bash his little pea head in with a shovel.

00:08:59.099 --> 00:09:01.920
(gentle music)

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.430
- Mom?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:07.320
- I was going to write screw
you bitches on the toes,

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.920
but I wasn't sure there'd be enough room.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.757
I hope they fit.
(gentle music)

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:29.260
- Feast your eyes, my
official Denton student ID.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:33.221
You can now call me
Denton Student 9783210.

00:09:33.221 --> 00:09:35.634
- Aww, honey.
- Look at that smile.

00:09:35.634 --> 00:09:38.810
- This is so exciting.
- Yeah it is.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:40.490
- Casey, take a picture of us.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:43.020
- Okay, No reason I should be in it,

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.320
as a member of this family.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.163
Beautiful.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.640
- Honey why aren't you eating?

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:51.320
- I have a stomach ache.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.713
- Oh, I see.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.030
- What do you see?

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.630
Why are you saying it like that?

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:00.130
- Nothing, it's just that
ever since you were little,

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:01.630
whenever you get stressed about something

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:03.380
you get a tummy ache.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.850
First dance recital, tummy ache.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.330
Kindergarten spelling bee, tummy ache.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:13.140
First ever track meet, you
guessed it folks, tummy ache.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.680
- Can someone pass the peas please?

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.390
- I'm just saying as someone who has known

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:20.690
your tummy since it was
born, it's a pattern.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.130
- Can I borrow these
because there's a noise

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:23.790
in here that's bothering me.
- No.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.070
- Yeah, I just need them for a sec.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.040
Come on we share stuff.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.490
- These are mine!
- Come on.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:32.593
Carry on.

00:10:32.593 --> 00:10:33.700
- I'm going to go find a doctor

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.750
to see when we can get out of here, okay?

00:10:39.758 --> 00:10:44.758
- Ya know, no one really knows
what causes appendicitis.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:45.603
- Stop.

00:10:45.603 --> 00:10:48.450
- So technically, it could
very well still be stress.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:49.310
- Stop.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.190
- Feeling torn between
two people, perhaps?

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.173
- Nurse, this lady banged a bartender!

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.480
- School called.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.940
You punched a milkshake?

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.947
- Um no, I didn't punch it, I bopped it.

00:10:59.947 --> 00:11:00.780
(clattering)
(flittering)

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:01.810
Like that.
(yells)

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:02.643
- Casey!

00:11:02.643 --> 00:11:05.450
- Ooh, that always makes a
bigger mess than I think it will.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.450
- Hey, what's going on?

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.700
- Casey punched a milkshake and my folder.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:10.960
- I'm living in the dorms.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.220
- Yeah?

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:15.430
Wow, I loved living in the dorm.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.350
What do you mean punched a milkshake?

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.800
- You have to stop punching things.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:20.633
- I agree.

00:11:20.633 --> 00:11:21.466
- Oh, do you?

00:11:21.466 --> 00:11:23.040
Because someone punched
a hole in the wall.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.480
Maybe we can hang a Merry Christmas sign

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.270
on Nate's milkshake.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.103
'Kay, bye.

00:11:27.103 --> 00:11:28.640
- Yeah, you better ''Kay, bye.'

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:32.160
- You're trying not to, but
you're smiling so big right now.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:32.993
- No, I'm not.

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:35.483
Hey, Casey.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.090
It was sweet of you to go to
Denton with your brother today.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.933
- I have no idea what
you're talking about.

00:11:41.933 --> 00:11:44.720
- I get it, you just had to help.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.920
You know, you're not as different

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.700
from me as you'd like to believe.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:51.340
- That is the meanest thing
you've ever said to me.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:52.940
And I'm not above bopping that tea.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.183
- Oh, I know you're not.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.200
- Why are we here?

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.010
- I know, I'm a monster.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.430
If I'm feeling really evil,

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.633
I'll take you to a fancy lunch after.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.500
How are you feeling honey?

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.903
- Not bad for a heartless garbage person.

00:12:10.513 --> 00:12:14.520
- I know, breakups are so hard.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:17.690
You made a kind and brave choice.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.260
I'd like to think I'd make that choice,

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:22.425
but we both know I'm not that strong.

00:12:22.425 --> 00:12:26.840
- Mom.

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.190
I mean it does really suck.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.730
And maybe it was the right thing to do,

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.773
but I just can't get him out of my head.

00:12:37.496 --> 00:12:39.843
It sucks.

00:12:39.843 --> 00:12:41.043
- [Elsa] I know it does.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.650
I may have something to
make you feel better.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:49.270
Check it out, Casey rocks!

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.873
For your track meet!

00:12:50.873 --> 00:12:53.440
This is gonna look great
in fingerless gloves?

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.290
- [Casey] Nothing looks
good in fingerless gloves.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:58.310
- [Elsa] Uh huh, Casey rocks!
- [Casey] Oh my god.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:01.135
- [Elsa] Casey Rocks!
- [Casey] Calm down!

00:13:01.135 --> 00:13:02.635
- [Elsa] Woo-woo!

